# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file the repo had no policy at all: core.autocrlf unset, HEAD
# stored as LF, and an editor writing CRLF into the working tree. The result was
# `git status` reporting 47 modified files and `git diff` showing 10,877
# insertions against 10,810 deletions — of which the real content change was 13
# files and 217 insertions. Everything else was carriage returns.
#
# Committing in that state would have buried every real change under a
# whole-tree whitespace rewrite and destroyed `git blame` for the entire engine.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF *in the repository* while leaving the working
# tree alone, so Windows checkouts still get CRLF and the churn is simply never
# recorded.
* text=auto

# Interpreters that care about their own line endings, regardless of platform.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.onnx binary
*.wav  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
